  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Multiplexer (data selector)"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A multiplexer (MUX) has $2^n$ data inputs, $n$ select lines and one output. The binary number on the select lines decides which input is connected to the output. For a 4:1 MUX, $Y = \\bar{S_1}\\bar{S_0}I_0 + \\bar{S_1}S_0I_1 + S_1\\bar{S_0}I_2 + S_1S_0I_3$. It is built from AND gates (one per input, enabled by one select combination) feeding an OR gate. ICs: 74151 (8:1), 74153 (dual 4:1). Uses: data selection, parallel-to-serial conversion, realising Boolean functions."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "2ⁿ inputs, n select lines, 1 output"
    },
    {
     "en": "Many-to-one: also called a data selector"
    },
    {
     "en": "IC 74151 is an 8:1 MUX"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A multiplexer is a data selector. With n select lines it chooses one of two to the power n inputs and connects it to the single output.",
    "kn": "ಮಲ್ಟಿಪ್ಲೆಕ್ಸರ್ ಒಂದು ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಆಯ್ಕೆಗಾರ. n ಆಯ್ಕೆ ರೇಖೆಗಳಿಂದ 2ⁿ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಒಂದನ್ನು ಆರಿಸಿ ಏಕೈಕ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗೆ ಜೋಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "formula": "Y = \\bar{S_1}\\bar{S_0}I_0 + \\bar{S_1}S_0I_1 + S_1\\bar{S_0}I_2 + S_1S_0I_3"
  },
