  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Demultiplexer (data distributor)"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A demultiplexer (DEMUX) does the reverse: one data input D, $n$ select lines and $2^n$ outputs. The select code decides which output receives D; all others stay 0. For a 1:4 DEMUX, $Y_0 = D\\bar{S_1}\\bar{S_0}$, $Y_1 = D\\bar{S_1}S_0$, $Y_2 = DS_1\\bar{S_0}$, $Y_3 = DS_1S_0$. A decoder with an enable input works as a demultiplexer (e.g. IC 74155). Uses: serial-to-parallel conversion, sending data to one of many destinations."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "1 input, n select lines, 2ⁿ outputs"
    },
    {
     "en": "One-to-many: also called a data distributor"
    },
    {
     "en": "MUX at the sender + DEMUX at the receiver share one line"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A demultiplexer is a data distributor. One input goes to one of two to the power n outputs, chosen by the select lines.",
    "kn": "ಡಿಮಲ್ಟಿಪ್ಲೆಕ್ಸರ್ ಒಂದು ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ವಿತರಕ. ಆಯ್ಕೆ ರೇಖೆಗಳು ಆರಿಸಿದ 2ⁿ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಒಂದಕ್ಕೆ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಹೋಗುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
